    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27426" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δί-πῠλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>double-gated, with two
				entrances,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				952
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίπυλον, τό,</span> a name for the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θριάσιαι πύλαι</span> at Athens, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				16.25.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Per.</u>
				30
			</span></i>; at Rome for the temple of Janus, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.322a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερῷον</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
